Cancer is a group of diseases involving uncontrolled cell growth typically resulting in tumors with the potential to invade or spread to other parts of the body.^{[2]}^{[8]} These malignant tumors contrast with benign tumors, which do not spread.^{[8]} Over 100 types of cancers affect humans.^{[8]}^{[9]}

Cancers comprise a large family of diseases that involve abnormal cell growth with the potential to invade or spread to other parts of the body.^{[2]}^{[8]} They form a subset of neoplasms. A neoplasm or tumor is a group of cells that have undergone unregulated growth and will often form a mass or lump, but may be distributed diffusely.^{[30]}^{[8]}

